## Controls and limits

One fixed runtime executable path, one fresh private repository/run directory
and memory custody process per source; one spawn and exactly one DM each.
Both use --ctl --run-dir <private> --quit-after 180.
Both builds use one private dev target, CARGO_BUILD_JOBS=2, cargo build
--locked -p bboxy450-term --bin bboxy450-term.
The first app closes and recorded descendants are absent before the next app.
No screen/desktop driving, trust approval, terminal input, follow-up ping,
ambiguous native-write retry, native client upgrade or manual global config edit.

This is a functional comparison under observed shared-host load, not a quiet
latency benchmark. The aea build starts after the first reply was observed.
Old polling was interrupted by a process disappearing between ps inventory
and ps command lookup. The initial driver exits 1 for this harness error.
Read-only observation resumes against the SAME app/seat/challenge, sends no
second DM, and finds the correlated reply. The old reply envelope timestamp
is approximately 13 seconds after DM, at one-second timestamp resolution;
48.612 seconds is the observed upper bound after the polling interruption.
The resumed observer exits 0. The new driver handles that ps race and exits 0.

The reported regression is NOT reproduced by these short-message controls.
The Oracle role prompt alone is not sufficient to reproduce it here.
The original approximately 7 KB first DM followed by a ping was NOT tested,
nor was its task content copied. No causal attribution to size, role or merge
is made, and no product fix is authorized by this result.

